{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88e7932e365e14f2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tspec: [\"001-sentry-analyzer-repo-map-and-lineno-less-frames\"]\n3\tstatus: draft\n4\tcreated: \"2026-09-01T13:00:00Z\"\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t<summary>\n8\t- The Sentry reader no longer reports \"no stack trace\" when a stack trace actually exists but its frames lack line numbers\n9\t- Events whose exception entry carries at least one frame now always emit the frames: `file:line in function` when a line number is usable, otherwise `basename in function`\n10\t- Events whose exception entry exists but has zero frames now get a distinct \"no frames\" marker instead of the misleading \"no exception entry\" message\n11\t- \"No exception entry\" is now reserved for events that genuinely lack an exception entry\n12\t- Frame values are forced onto a single line so a crafted frame can no longer inject fake lines into the output block\n13\t- Existing behavior is untouched: metadata key order, the 30-frame cap, mixed-line-number frames, and the timeout/auth/fetch-failure markers all work as before\n14\t- The deterministic mock-API test gains a lineno-less fixture and an empty-frames fixture and now prints \"PASS: all AC1-AC6 assertions passed\"\n15\t- The changelog gains an \"Unreleased\" entry documenting the new frame-emission contract\n16\t</summary>\n17\t\n18\t<objective>\n19\tMake `scripts/sentry-read.sh` report the latest event's stack trace truthfully: emit frames whenever an exception entry carries them (including when none have a usable line number), reserve `stack_trace unavailable (no exception entry)` for events that genuinely lack an exception entry, add a distinct `stack_trace unavailable (no frames)` marker, and keep every emitted frame value single-line — all locked by new deterministic mock-API fixtures in `scripts/test-sentry-read.sh`.\n20\t</objective>\n21\t\n22\t<context>\n23\tRead CLAUDE.md for project conventions.\n24\t\n25\tRead `scripts/sentry-read.sh` in full. The code to change is the python3 `-c` extraction block inside the `else` branch of the event-fetch classification: the block bound to `frames=\"$(python3 -c '...' \"${event_body}\")\"`, followed by the `if [ \"${frames_rc}\" -ne 0 ] || [ -z \"${frames}\" ]` fallback. The `set +e` / `set -e` guard around it, the curl classification above it (timeout / 404 → `no events` / 401+403 → `auth` / other → `fetch failed`), and the 7-key metadata block must remain unchanged.\n26\t\n27\tRead `scripts/test-sentry-read.sh` in full. The fixture server's `event_latest(self, issue)` method (the existing `elif issue == \"999\"` branch is the insertion anchor), the `fail()` helper, and the `check_failure` helper show the patterns to follow. The final line `echo \"PASS: all AC1-AC5 assertions passed\"` must become `AC1-AC6`.\n28\t\n29\tRead `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/changelog-guide.md` for the changelog entry format.\n30\t</context>\n31\t\n32\t<requirements>\n33\t1. In `scripts/sentry-read.sh`, replace the entire python3 `-c` extraction block inside the `else` branch. Keep the `set +e` / `set -e` guard and the trailing shell fallback exactly as they are:\n34\t\n35\t   ```bash\n36\t   if [ \"${frames_rc}\" -ne 0 ] || [ -z \"${frames}\" ]; then\n37\t     printf 'stack_trace unavailable (no exception entry)\\n'\n38\t   else\n39\t     printf '%s\\n' \"${frames}\"\n40\t   fi\n41\t   ```\n42\t\n43\t   This fallback now fires only when python exits non-zero or produces empty output — a malformed/partial event body, which is pre-existing behavior (spec failure-mode \"partial event body\"; the reason enum is frozen to `timeout | no events | auth | fetch failed | no frames | no exception entry`, do NOT add a new reason string). <!-- REVIEW NOTE: on a 200 response whose body fails to parse (truncated download), the python block exits with empty output and the shell fallback emits `no exception entry` (pre-existing best-effort behavior; the spec freezes the reason enum to `timeout | no events | auth | fetch failed | no frames | no exception entry` and its Failure-Modes row for a partial body asks only for a best-effort marker). If you consider that marker still misleading for truncated bodies, veto this choice and require a dedicated fixture -- otherwise leave as-is. --> Replace only the python source inside the single-quoted heredoc with exactly this block — the three-state classification is load-bearing, do not paraphrase it. The fenced code blocks in this prompt are indented 3 spaces because they sit inside numbered-list items. When you copy a block into a script, strip that list indentation: the python here must start flush-left at column 0 (module-level statements must not be indented, or Python raises IndentationError).\n44\t\n45\t   ```python\n46\t   import json, sys, os, re\n47\t   try:\n48\t       data = json.load(open(sys.argv[1]))\n49\t       exception_found = False\n50\t       frames = []\n51\t       for entry in data.get(\"entries\", []):\n52\t           if entry.get(\"type\") == \"exception\":\n53\t               exception_found = True\n54\t               values = entry.get(\"data\", {}).get(\"values\", [])\n55\t               if values:\n56\t                   frames = values[0].get(\"stacktrace\", {}).get(\"frames\", []) or []\n57\t               break\n58\t   except Exception:\n59\t       sys.exit(0)\n60\t   if not exception_found:\n61\t       print(\"stack_trace unavailable (no exception entry)\")\n62\t       sys.exit(0)\n63\t   if not frames:\n64\t       print(\"stack_trace unavailable (no frames)\")\n65\t       sys.exit(0)\n66\t   lineno_lines = []\n67\t   no_lineno_lines = []\n68\t   for frame in frames[:30]:\n69\t       path = (frame.get(\"abs_path\") or frame.get(\"filename\") or \"\").strip()\n70\t       func = (frame.get(\"function\") or \"unknown\").strip()\n71\t       # single-line: neutralise control chars so a crafted payload cannot inject lines\n72\t       path = re.sub(r\"[\\x00-\\x1f\\x7f]+\", \" \", path).strip()\n73\t       func = re.sub(r\"[\\x00-\\x1f\\x7f]+\", \" \", func).strip()\n74\t       lineno = frame.get(\"lineno\")\n75\t       if isinstance(lineno, int):\n76\t           lineno_lines.append(\"%s:%s in %s\" % (os.path.basename(path), lineno, func))\n77\t       else:\n78\t           no_lineno_lines.append(\"%s in %s\" % (os.path.basename(path), func))\n79\t   emitted = lineno_lines if lineno_lines else no_lineno_lines\n80\t   print(\"stack_trace=%d frames\" % len(emitted))\n81\t   print(\"\\n\".join(emitted))\n82\t   ```\n83\t\n84\t   The block classifies a successful (HTTP 200) fetch into exactly one output state:\n85\t   - An exception entry exists and its first value's `stacktrace.frames` has ≥1 element → print a `stack_trace=<N> frames` header, then one line per emitted frame (≤30, via `frames[:30]`): `basename:lineno in function` when `lineno` is an integer, otherwise `basename in function`. `N` is the number of emitted frame lines.\n86\t   - An exception entry exists but its first value's `stacktrace.frames` is empty or missing → print `stack_trace unavailable (no frames)`.\n87\t   - No exception entry → print `stack_trace unavailable (no exception entry)`.\n88\t\n89\t   Behavior rules that must hold (spec Desired Behaviors 1–4 and Failure Modes):\n90\t   - Mixed frames (some with a usable integer `lineno`, some without): only the frames with a usable integer `lineno` are emitted as `file:line in function`; the others are dropped — current behavior unchanged, no new regression surface.\n91\t   - `lineno` present but a string (schema drift, e.g. `\"42\"`) is treated as lineno-less → emitted as `basename in function` — never a false `no exception entry`.\n92\t   - Single-line guarantee: C0 control characters (`\\x00`–`\\x1f`) and DEL (`\\x7f`), including `\\n`/`\\r`, are replaced with a single space in both the basename and function before the line is built, so a crafted `function`/`filename` cannot inject extra lines into the output block (Security failure mode).\n93\t   - No-PII: only `abs_path`/`filename` basename and `function` are emitted — never `context`, never the raw payload.\n94\t   - The `except Exception: sys.exit(0)` parse-failure path is unchanged; the spec's reason enum stays exactly `timeout | no events | auth | fetch failed | no frames | no exception entry`.\n95\t\n96\t2. Update the comment blocks in `scripts/sentry-read.sh` that describe the output contract:\n97\t   - The header comment at the top (the lines listing the emitted block and the `stack_trace unavailable (<reason>)` reasons) must document: the two frame line shapes (`<file>:<line> in <function>` and `<basename> in <function>`), the reason enum `timeout | no events | auth | fetch failed | no frames | no exception entry`, the three-state classification (frames are emitted whenever an exception entry carries ≥1 frame; `no frames` is emitted only when an exception entry exists with zero frames; `no exception entry` only when no exception entry exists), and the single-line guarantee.\n98\t   - The inline comment above the python block in the `else` branch (currently \"HTTP 200: extract only filename/abs_path basename...\") must mention the three-state classification.\n99\t\n100\t3. In `scripts/test-sentry-read.sh`:\n101\t   a. Add two fixtures to the fixture server's `event_latest(self, issue)` method, directly after the existing `elif issue == \"999\"` branch (the `metadata()` method already serves any issue id, so no metadata change is needed). The following block is indented to sit inside the numbered list — copy it into `event_latest(self, issue)` with `elif` branches at 8 spaces and their bodies at 12 spaces, exactly matching the existing `elif issue == \"999\"` branch:\n102\t\n103\t   ```python\n104\t   elif issue == \"222\":\n105\t       # Lineno-less frames (real nuke shape: issue 6727724202). None has an\n106\t       # integer lineno; frame 4 carries a string lineno (\"42\") to lock the\n107\t       # schema-drift path; frame 5 carries a newline+equals in `function`\n108\t       # to lock single-line stripping.\n109\t       self._send(200, {\"entries\": [\n110\t           {\"type\": \"exception\", \"data\": {\"values\": [\n111\t               {\"stacktrace\": {\"frames\": [\n112\t                   {\"filename\": \"kafka/coordinator/consumer.py\", \"abs_path\": None, \"lineno\": None, \"function\": \"_maybe_auto_commit_offsets_sync\", \"context\": [\"RAW-CONTEXT-SENTINEL line 1\"]},\n113\t                   {\"filename\": \"kafka/protocol/fetch.py\", \"abs_path\": None, \"lineno\": None, \"function\": \"FetchRequest\", \"context\": [\"RAW-CONTEXT-SENTINEL line 2\"]},\n114\t                   {\"filename\": \"kafka/consumer/group.py\", \"abs_path\": None, \"lineno\": None, \"function\": \"_poll_once\", \"context\": [\"RAW-CONTEXT-SENTINEL line 3\"]},\n115\t                   {\"filename\": \"nuke/worker.py\", \"abs_path\": None, \"lineno\": \"42\", \"function\": \"sync_worker\", \"context\": [\"RAW-CONTEXT-SENTINEL line 4\"]},\n116\t                   {\"filename\": \"nuke/backlog.py\", \"abs_path\": None, \"lineno\": None, \"function\": \"dispatch\\nCOUNT=999\", \"context\": [\"RAW-CONTEXT-SENTINEL line 5\"]},\n117\t               ]}}\n118\t           ]}}\n119\t       ]})\n120\t   elif issue == \"333\":\n121\t       # Exception entry whose first value's stacktrace has zero frames.\n122\t       self._send(200, {\"entries\": [\n123\t           {\"type\": \"exception\", \"data\": {\"values\": [\n124\t               {\"stacktrace\": {\"frames\": []}}\n125\t           ]}}\n126\t       ]})\n127\t   ```\n128\t\n129\t   b. After the existing AC4 failure-path assertions (the `check_failure \"AC4 auth (401)\" ...` block) and before the final `echo \"PASS: ...\"` line, add these assertions (they lock AC2 + the schema-drift and single-line failure modes for issue 222, and AC6 for issue 333; `check_failure` already asserts the 7 metadata keys and exactly one marker). The following block is indented to sit inside the numbered list — copy it into the test script using the file's 2-space indentation convention (top-level statements at 2 spaces, nested bodies at 4):\n130\t\n131\t   ```bash\n132\t   # ---- AC2: lineno-less frames emitted truthfully (issue 222) ----\n133\t   if ! out_nolineno=\"$(bash \"${SCRIPT}\" 222 2>&1)\"; then\n134\t     fail \"AC2 lineno-less fixture exited non-zero\"\n135\t   fi\n136\t   key_count=\"$(printf '%s\\n' \"${out_nolineno}\" | grep -cE '^(short_id|status|live_event_count|first_seen|last_seen|users_impacted|title)=' || true)\"\n137\t   if [ \"${key_count}\" -ne 7 ]; then\n138\t     fail \"AC2 lineno-less fixture expected 7 metadata keys, got ${key_count}\"\n139\t   fi\n140\t   nl_header=\"$(printf '%s\\n' \"${out_nolineno}\" | grep -cE '^stack_trace=[1-9][0-9]* frames$' || true)\"\n141\t   if [ \"${nl_header}\" -ne 1 ]; then\n142\t     fail \"AC2 lineno-less fixture expected exactly one 'stack_trace=<N> frames' header, got ${nl_header}\"\n143\t   fi\n144\t   if ! printf '%s\\n' \"${out_nolineno}\" | grep -q '^stack_trace=5 frames$'; then\n145\t     fail \"AC2 lineno-less fixture expected 'stack_trace=5 frames' header\"\n146\t   fi\n147\t   nl_frames=\"$(printf '%s\\n' \"${out_nolineno}\" | grep -cE '^[^=]+ in ' || true)\"\n148\t   if [ \"${nl_frames}\" -ne 5 ]; then\n149\t     fail \"AC2 lineno-less fixture expected 5 'basename in function' frame lines, got ${nl_frames}\"\n150\t   fi\n151\t   if ! printf '%s\\n' \"${out_nolineno}\" | grep -q '^consumer.py in _maybe_auto_commit_offsets_sync$'; then\n152\t     fail \"AC2 lineno-less frame format mismatch (expected 'consumer.py in _maybe_auto_commit_offsets_sync')\"\n153\t   fi\n154\t   if ! printf '%s\\n' \"${out_nolineno}\" | grep -q '^worker.py in sync_worker$'; then\n155\t     fail \"AC2 string-lineno frame not treated as lineno-less (expected 'worker.py in sync_worker')\"\n156\t   fi\n157\t   if printf '%s\\n' \"${out_nolineno}\" | grep -qE ':[0-9]+ in '; then\n158\t     fail \"AC2 lineno-less fixture leaked a ':line' frame\"\n159\t   fi\n160\t   if printf '%s\\n' \"${out_nolineno}\" | grep -q 'no exception entry'; then\n161\t     fail \"AC2 lineno-less fixture emitted 'no exception entry' despite frames existing\"\n162\t   fi\n163\t   if printf '%s\\n' \"${out_nolineno}\" | grep -q 'no frames'; then\n164\t     fail \"AC2 lineno-less fixture emitted 'no frames' despite frames existing\"\n165\t   fi\n166\t   if printf '%s\\n' \"${out_nolineno}\" | grep -qE '\"context\"|\"frames\"|stacktrace'; then\n167\t     fail \"AC4 raw JSON keys leaked from lineno-less fixture\"\n168\t   fi\n169\t   if printf '%s\\n' \"${out_nolineno}\" | grep -q 'RAW-CONTEXT-SENTINEL'; then\n170\t     fail \"AC4 fixture context sentinel leaked from lineno-less fixture\"\n171\t   fi\n172\t   if ! printf '%s\\n' \"${out_nolineno}\" | grep -q '^backlog.py in dispatch COUNT=999$'; then\n173\t     fail \"AC4 newline in frame function was not neutralised to a single line\"\n174\t   fi\n175\t   if printf '%s\\n' \"${out_nolineno}\" | grep -q '^COUNT=999$'; then\n176\t     fail \"AC4 newline in frame function injected a standalone line\"\n177\t   fi\n178\t\n179\t   # ---- AC6: no-frames marker distinct from no-exception-entry (issue 333) ----\n180\t   if ! out_noframes=\"$(bash \"${SCRIPT}\" 333 2>&1)\"; then\n181\t     fail \"AC6 no-frames stub exited non-zero\"\n182\t   fi\n183\t   check_failure \"AC6 no frames\" \"${out_noframes}\" \"no frames\"\n184\t   if printf '%s\\n' \"${out_noframes}\" | grep -q 'no exception entry'; then\n185\t     fail \"AC6 no-frames stub emitted 'no exception entry' instead of 'no frames'\"\n186\t   fi\n187\t   ```\n188\t\n189\t   c. Change the final line to `echo \"PASS: all AC1-AC6 assertions passed\"`.\n190\t   d. Update the test file's header comment so its spec reference points at `specs/in-progress/001-sentry-analyzer-repo-map-and-lineno-less-frames.md` and its AC summary mentions the new lineno-less (AC2) and empty-frames (AC6) fixtures. Do NOT weaken any existing assertion (metadata order, 30-frame cap on issue-123, failure stubs 456/789/999).\n191\t\n192\t4. Add a fresh `## Unreleased` section at the very top of `CHANGELOG.md` (above the current `## v0.8.0` section; if a `## Unreleased` section already exists, append to it rather than duplicating) with one `fix:` entry describing the frame-emission contract change: `scripts/sentry-read.sh` now emits frames whenever an exception entry carries them — including when none have a usable line number (as `basename in function`), emits the distinct `stack_trace unavailable (no frames)` marker for an exception entry with zero frames, reserves `stack_trace unavailable (no exception entry)` for events with no exception entry, and neutralises control characters in emitted frame values so every frame line stays single-line. Follow the format in `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/changelog-guide.md`.\n193\t\n194\t5. Before finishing, re-run `<verification>` and confirm it passes; walk acceptance criteria AC2, AC3, AC4, AC6 and the bash-test part of AC5 against your change.\n195\t</requirements>\n196\t\n197\t<constraints>\n198\t- Do NOT commit — dark-factory handles git.\n199\t- The metadata block contract is frozen: exactly the 7 key=value lines (`short_id`, `status`, `live_event_count`, `first_seen`, `last_seen`, `users_impacted`, `title`) in their current order; a metadata fetch failure still exits non-zero.\n200\t- The event fetch stays best-effort and non-fatal: it never fails the run and degrades to exactly one `stack_trace unavailable (<reason>)` line; the reason enum is exactly `timeout | no events | auth | fetch failed | no frames | no exception entry` — do NOT add new reason strings.\n201\t- No-PII is a hard invariant for both frame shapes: basename only, no context lines, no raw payload, capped 30 frames; every emitted frame value is single-line (control characters neutralised).\n202\t- Mixed-case frames (some with a usable integer `lineno`, some without) keep current behavior: only the frames with a usable `lineno` are emitted as `file:line in function` — no new regression surface.\n203\t- `scripts/repo-clone.sh`, the execution / deep-execution prompts, the verdict logic, and the `<output-format>` contract are untouched by this prompt.\n204\t- The existing `scripts/test-sentry-read.sh` assertions for metadata order, the 30-frame cap on the issue-123 fixture, and the failure stubs (456 no-exception / 789 404 / 999 401) must still pass without weakening.\n205\t- Do NOT create a new scenario file — the mock-API test plus the operator live probe cover the behavior (spec non-goal).\n206\t- This prompt changes no Go code — do not edit any `.go` file.\n207\t- Existing tests must still pass.\n208\t</constraints>\n209\t\n210\t<verification>\n211\tThis prompt changes no Go code, so `make precommit` is NOT required. Verify with:\n212\t\n213\t- `bash scripts/test-sentry-read.sh` — must exit 0 and print `PASS: all AC1-AC6 assertions passed` (covers AC2/AC3/AC4/AC6 and preserves the existing AC1-AC5 assertions)\n214\t- `grep '## Unreleased' CHANGELOG.md` — must match the new section\n215\t</verification>\n216\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87d319a06106acdb","session_id":"bf6eb875-41e8-4988-a539-5dee3a13bc7d","uuid":"ef8fddcd-f4f7-4f8b-bcc6-cbb5870de020","timestamp":"2026-09-01T12:22:08.938Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Create prompts from spec"}
