{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a23cd4b9d821a49","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tspec: [\"001-sentry-analyzer-repo-map-and-lineno-less-frames\"]\n3\tstatus: draft\n4\tcreated: \"2026-09-01T13:10:00Z\"\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t<summary>\n8\t- The triage planning prompt now maps Sentry projects `nuke-dev` and `nuke-prod` to the source repo `bborbe/nuke`\n9\t- The deep planning prompt carries the same mapping note in its clone step\n10\t- The canonical repo is tried before any project-named guess when the stack trace lacks a repo path\n11\t- The mapping stays a short, general note — not a table of every Sentry project\n12\t- Go prompt tests assert both embedded planning prompts contain the mapping, so a regression fails `go test ./pkg/prompts/...`\n13\t- The changelog gains an \"Unreleased\" entry documenting the mapping guidance\n14\t</summary>\n15\t\n16\t<objective>\n17\tAnchor the nuke project→repo mapping (`nuke-dev` / `nuke-prod` → `bborbe/nuke`) in the clone step of both analyzer planning prompts so the agent clones the canonical repo before guessing project-named variants when the stack trace lacks a repo path, and lock it with Go prompt-test assertions.\n18\t</objective>\n19\t\n20\t<context>\n21\tRead CLAUDE.md for project conventions.\n22\t\n23\tRead `pkg/prompts/planning.md` in full — the note goes in Step 3, immediately after the `Bash(scripts/repo-clone.sh clone <repo>)` line, before the blank line / the paragraph starting \"where `<repo>` is the owner/name\".\n24\t\n25\tRead `pkg/prompts/deep-planning.md` in full — the note goes in Step 2, immediately after the `Bash(scripts/repo-clone.sh clone <repo>)` line, before the blank line / the paragraph starting \"where `<repo>` is the owner/name\".\n26\t\n27\tRead `pkg/prompts/prompts.go` — the `//go:embed` variables and the `BuildPlanningInstructions` / `BuildDeepPlanningInstructions` functions (do NOT modify this file; it needs no structural change).\n28\t\n29\tRead `pkg/prompts/prompts_test.go` — the Ginkgo/Gomega assertion pattern. Add new `It` blocks inside the existing `Describe(\"BuildPlanningInstructions (triage)\"` and `Describe(\"BuildDeepPlanningInstructions\"` blocks, following the existing `It(\"planning prompt contains the read-only repo clone invocation\", ...)` pattern (which asserts on `instrs[0].Content`).\n30\t\n31\tRead `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/changelog-guide.md` and `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md`.\n32\t</context>\n33\t\n34\t<requirements>\n35\t1. In `pkg/prompts/planning.md`, Step 3, insert this note as a single line directly after the `Bash(scripts/repo-clone.sh clone <repo>)` line (before the blank line and the \"where `<repo>` is the owner/name\" paragraph). The `bborbe/nuke` text must fall within 5 lines after the clone-invocation line (AC1 evidence: `grep -A5 'repo-clone.sh clone' pkg/prompts/planning.md | grep -c 'bborbe/nuke'` ≥ 1):\n36\t\n37\t   ```\n38\t   Sentry projects `nuke-dev` and `nuke-prod` map to source repo `bborbe/nuke`; when the stack trace lacks a repo path (frames are external library code with no bborbe repo path), clone the mapped canonical repo `bborbe/nuke` before guessing a project-named variant like `nuke-dev`.\n39\t   ```\n40\t\n41\t   The note must contain `nuke-dev`, `nuke-prod`, and `bborbe/nuke`, and must stay a minimal general note — NOT a table of every Sentry project (spec invariant).\n42\t\n43\t2. In `pkg/prompts/deep-planning.md`, Step 2, insert the same note (identical wording) as a single line directly after the `Bash(scripts/repo-clone.sh clone <repo>)` line, before the blank line and the \"where `<repo>` is the owner/name\" paragraph (AC1 evidence: `grep -A5 'repo-clone.sh clone' pkg/prompts/deep-planning.md | grep -c 'bborbe/nuke'` ≥ 1).\n44\t\n45\t3. In `pkg/prompts/prompts_test.go`, add two `It` blocks following the existing Ginkgo/Gomega pattern (which calls `prompts.BuildPlanningInstructions()` / `prompts.BuildDeepPlanningInstructions()` and asserts on `instrs[0].Content`):\n46\t   - Inside `Describe(\"BuildPlanningInstructions (triage)\", ...)`: `It(\"planning prompt contains the nuke repo-mapping guidance\", ...)` asserting the planning content `ContainSubstring(\"nuke-dev\")` and `ContainSubstring(\"bborbe/nuke\")`.\n47\t   - Inside `Describe(\"BuildDeepPlanningInstructions\", ...)`: `It(\"deep planning prompt contains the nuke repo-mapping guidance\", ...)` asserting the deep-planning content `ContainSubstring(\"nuke-dev\")` and `ContainSubstring(\"bborbe/nuke\")`.\n48\t\n49\t   These assertions traverse the `//go:embed` boundary — they read the embedded markdown through the same `Build*Instructions` accessors the runtime uses, so an embedded-prompt edit that drops the mapping fails the test.\n50\t\n51\t4. Append the mapping-guidance entry to the `## Unreleased` section of `CHANGELOG.md`: if `## Unreleased` exists (created by the frame-contract prompt), append a new `feat:` bullet to it; if it is absent (this prompt may run first), create `## Unreleased` at the top of the file above `## v0.8.0` and add the bullet. The entry: the analyzer planning prompts (`planning.md`, `deep-planning.md`) now map Sentry projects `nuke-dev` / `nuke-prod` to the source repo `bborbe/nuke` and instruct the agent to clone the canonical repo before guessing project-named variants when the stack trace lacks a repo path. Follow the format in `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/changelog-guide.md`.\n52\t\n53\t5. Before finishing, re-run `<verification>` and confirm it passes; walk acceptance criterion AC1 against your change.\n54\t</requirements>\n55\t\n56\t<constraints>\n57\t- Do NOT commit — dark-factory handles git.\n58\t- The mapping guidance is a note, not a project table — do NOT add a table of every Sentry project (spec invariant).\n59\t- Do NOT change `scripts/repo-clone.sh` or anything else under `scripts/`.\n60\t- Prompts stay Go-embedded via `//go:embed`; `pkg/prompts/prompts.go` requires no structural change — only markdown content in `pkg/prompts/planning.md` / `pkg/prompts/deep-planning.md` and test additions to `pkg/prompts/prompts_test.go`.\n61\t- Do NOT touch the execution / deep-execution prompts, the collector-planning prompt, the verdict logic, the `<output-format>` contract, or `scripts/sentry-read.sh`.\n62\t- Existing tests must still pass.\n63\t- Do NOT create a new scenario file — container-executable tests cover the behavior (spec non-goal).\n64\t- No new config knobs, flags, or thresholds — the mapping note is static markdown.\n65\t</constraints>\n66\t\n67\t<verification>\n68\t- `go test -mod=mod ./pkg/prompts/...` — must exit 0\n69\t- `grep -A5 'repo-clone.sh clone' pkg/prompts/planning.md | grep -c 'bborbe/nuke'` — must be ≥ 1\n70\t- `grep -A5 'repo-clone.sh clone' pkg/prompts/deep-planning.md | grep -c 'bborbe/nuke'` — must be ≥ 1\n71\t- `grep '## Unreleased' CHANGELOG.md` — must match\n72\t- `make precommit` — must pass (this prompt changes Go test code)\n73\t</verification>\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87d319a06106acdb","session_id":"bf6eb875-41e8-4988-a539-5dee3a13bc7d","uuid":"a9bd7df6-a82b-4cf0-8880-ebe4f7634c79","timestamp":"2026-09-01T12:22:10.134Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Create prompts from spec"}
