me/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md` (prompt 2)\n\nNo reusable pattern was inlined that lacks a doc — the mock-API fixture technique is already established in the existing `test-sentry-read.sh`, so no new doc suggested.\n\n### Open questions surfaced inside the prompts\n\nOne `<!-- REVIEW NOTE -->` HTML comment in prompt 1 requirement 1: on a 200 response whose body fails to parse (truncated download), the shell fallback still emits `no exception entry` (pre-existing behavior; the spec freezes the reason enum and its partial-body failure mode asks only for a \"best-effort marker\"). I chose to keep it as-is — adding a `parse failed` reason would be scope creep beyond the spec's frozen enum. The comment invites the reviewer to veto if they consider that marker still misleading for truncated bodies.\n\n### Verification approach per prompt\n\n- Prompt 1: no Go code changed → skips `make precommit` (per global rule); verifies with `bash scripts/test-sentry-read.sh` + `grep '## Unreleased' CHANGELOG.md`.\n- Prompt 2: Go test code changed → `go test -mod=mod ./pkg/prompts/...`, the two AC1 greps, the changelog grep, then `make precommit`.\n\nSuggest: run `/audit-prompt /workspace/prompts/1-spec-001-sentry-read-frame-contract.md` and `/audit-prompt /workspace/prompts/2-spec-001-repo-mapping-guidance.md` before approving.","usage":{"total_tokens":0,"tool_uses":38,"duration_ms":364352},"uuid":"9b6cbbcf-3453-4e32-a454-b35bad708edf","session_id":"bf6eb875-41e8-4988-a539-5dee3a13bc7d"}
