{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-aae41c95902179de","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tspec: [\"001-sentry-analyzer-repo-map-and-lineno-less-frames\"]\n3\tstatus: draft\n4\tcreated: \"2026-09-01T13:10:00Z\"\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t<summary>\n8\t- The triage planning prompt now maps Sentry projects `nuke-dev` and `nuke-prod` to the source repo `bborbe/nuke`\n9\t- The deep planning prompt carries the same mapping note in its clone step\n10\t- The canonical repo is tried before any project-named guess when the stack trace lacks a repo path\n11\t- The mapping stays a short, general note — not a table of every Sentry project\n12\t- Go prompt tests assert both embedded planning prompts contain the mapping, so a regression fails `go test ./pkg/prompts/...`\n13\t- The changelog gains an \"Unreleased\" entry documenting the mapping guidance\n14\t</summary>\n15\t\n16\t<objective>\n17\tAnchor the nuke project→repo mapping (`nuke-dev` / `nuke-prod` → `bborbe/nuke`) in the clone step of both analyzer planning prompts so the agent clones the canonical repo before guessing project-named variants when the stack trace lacks a repo path, and lock it with Go prompt-test assertions.\n18\t</objective>\n19\t\n20\t<context>\n21\tRead CLAUDE.md for project conventions.\n22\t\n23\tRead `pkg/prompts/planning.md` in full — the note goes in Step 3, immediately after the `Bash(scripts/repo-clone.sh clone <repo>)` line, before the blank line / the paragraph starting \"where `<repo>` is the owner/name\".\n24\t\n25\tRead `pkg/prompts/deep-planning.md` in full — the note goes in Step 2, immediately after the `Bash(scripts/repo-clone.sh clone <repo>)` line, before the blank line / the paragraph starting \"where `<repo>` is the owner/name\".\n26\t\n27\tRead `pkg/prompts/prompts.go` — the `//go:embed` variables and the `BuildPlanningInstructions` / `BuildDeepPlanningInstructions` functions (do NOT modify this file; it needs no structural change).\n28\t\n