ectly pinned with verbatim blocks + explicit de-indentation instructions), not generic patterns that belong in a doc\n- [x] `changelog-guide.md` referenced in `<context>` (correct — no inline changelog formatting)\n- [x] Project `docs/` checked — no dedicated sentry-read doc exists to reference\n- [x] Changelog placement verified against changelog-guide: `## Unreleased` goes directly above `## v0.8.0` (line 5), immediately after the frozen header (lines 1-3); `fix:` prefix matches the guide's allowed prefix set\n\n## Code Reference Verification\nAll references verified against the actual sources.\n\n| Reference | File | Status |\n|-----------|------|--------|\n| `frames=\"$(python3 -c '...' \"${event_body}\")\"` + `frames_rc` + `[ -z \"${frames}\" ]` fallback (the \"else\" branch) | `scripts/sentry-read.sh:92-124` | Correct — exact anchor; python source is single-quoted heredoc, new block contains no apostrophes (no quoting hazard) |\n| `set +e`/`set -e` guard and curl classification (timeout/404/401/403/fetch failed) | `scripts/sentry-read.sh:67-87` | Correct — prompt marks it unchanged |\n| 7-key metadata block | `scripts/sentry-read.sh:52-59` | Correct — untouched |\n| Header comment (lines 8-16) listing frame shapes + reason enum | `scripts/sentry-read.sh:8-16` | Correct — currently missing `no frames` + lineno-less shape; req 2a addresses it |\n| Inline comment \"HTTP 200: extract only filename/abs_path basename...\" | `scripts/sentry-read.sh:89-90` | Correct — req 2b addresses it |\n| `event_latest(self, issue)` + `elif issue == \"999\"` insertion anchor + `metadata()` serves any id | `scripts/test-sentry-read.sh:89-106` | Correct — verified `metadata()` is reached for any numeric id via `do_GET` (line 113-116); 222/333 get metadata with no server change |\n| `fail()` helper and `check_failure` helper | `scripts/test-sentry-read.sh:27-30, 211-227` | Correct — `check_failure` asserts 7 keys + exactly one marker, matching prompt's description |\n| Final line `echo \"PASS: all AC1-AC5 assertions passed\"` | `scripts/test-sentry-read.sh:244` | Correct — req 3c changes it to AC1-AC6 |\n| Stale spec reference `specs/in-progress/001-sentry-read-event-payload.md` | `scripts/test-sentry-read.sh:7` | Correct — points at a non-existent spec; req 2d fixes it to the current spec (exists) |\n| `## v0.8.0` section; no `## Unreleased` present | `CHANGELOG.md:5` | Correct — req 4 creates it |\n| `changelog-guide.md` format | `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/changelog-guide.md` | Correct — `## Unreleased` directly above highest version, `fix:` prefix, insert after frozen header |\n| Spec `001-sentry-analyzer-repo-map-and-lineno-less-frames` | `specs/in-progress/001-sentry-analyzer-repo-map-and-lineno-less-frames.md` | Correct — frontmatter `spec:` matches full slug |\n\n**End-to-end empirical verification** (strongest check): I applied the prompt's inlined python block, both fixtures, the full assertion block, and the AC1-AC6 line to temp copies of both scripts exactly per the indentation instructions (python flush-left, `elif` at 8 spaces/body at 12, test top-level at 2/nested at 4), and ran the resulting test:\n\n```\nPASS: all AC1-AC6 assertions passed\nEXIT=0\n```\n\nThe pristine repo test passes (`PASS: all AC1-AC5 assertions passed`). The 222 fixture emits exactly:\n```\nstack_trace=5 frames\nconsumer.py in _maybe_auto_commit_offsets_sync\nfetch.py in FetchRequest\ngroup.py in _poll_once\nworker.py in sync_worker\nbacklog.py in dispatch COUNT=999\n```\nconfirming the string-`\"42\"` lineno is treated as lineno-less, the `dispatch\\nCOUNT=999` newline is neutralised to a single line, and no raw JSON / context sentinel leaks. The 333 fixture emits exactly `stack_trace unavailable (no frames)` and `check_failure` passes. The 123/456/789/999 assertions are preserved unchanged. I also verified the mixed-lineno precedence (`emitted = lineno_lines if lineno_lines else no_lineno_lines`) produces only the int-lineno frame at the python level.\n\n## Coding Guidelines Compliance\nNot applicable — the prompt changes zero Go code (constraints and `<verification>` both correctly state `make precommit` is not required). The only coding-guideline doc in play is `changelog-guide.md`, which is referenced and followed.\n\n## YAGNI Pass (scope-creep detector)\n- [x] No opt-out flag or escape hatch — no config knobs introduced\n- [x] No tunable thresholds beyond the spec-mandated 30-frame cap (pre-existing)\n- [x] No future-proofing knobs; the \"mixed-case frames keep current behavior\" rule is spec-mandated (constraint), not scope creep\n- [x] Reason enum is frozen to spec values; the prompt explicitly forbids adding new reason strings — no invented states\n\n## Critical Issues\nNone.\n\n## Recommendations\n\n**R1 — Mixed-lineno precedence branch is untested (new logic, no fixture).**\nPrompt line 79 introduces `emitted = lineno_lines if lineno_lines else no_lineno_lines` — a genuinely new two-list split plus a truthiness decision. The test set covers only the two degenerate ends: issue 123 (all frames have int `lineno` → `lineno_lines` non-empty) and issue 222 (no frame has an int `lineno` → `no_lineno_lines`). The mixed case — both lists non-empty, only `lineno_lines` emitted, `no_lineno_lines` dropped — has no fixture, so a future edit to the precedence (e.g. `lineno_lines + no_lineno_lines`) would pass every test while breaking the spec constraint \"Mixed-case frames ... only the frames with a usable `lineno` are emitted\". I confirmed the branch behaves correctly today, but it is un-locked.\n*Fix:* extend the 222 fixture (or add a small 444 fixture) with one frame carrying an integer `lineno` alongside the lineno-less ones, and assert the emitted lines contain exactly one `file:line in function` line and that the no-lineno frames are dropped.\n\n**R2 — AC-numbering collision in the test after the header retarget.**\nThe pre-existing assertion blocks in `scripts/test-sentry-read.sh` are labeled with the OLD spec's AC numbers (AC1 = 7 keys, AC2 = frame format, AC3 = bare/URL identical, AC4 = failure stubs, AC5 = cap/no-PII — lines 170-242), but req 2d retargets the header (lines 6-16) at the NEW spec, where those numbers mean different things (AC2 = lineno-less, AC3 = no-exception preserved, AC4 = no-PII+cap, AC6 = no-frames). After the change, the file will carry two blocks both labeled \"AC2\" and old-labeled blocks that contradict the new spec's AC map. This is inherited partly from the spec (the \"PASS: all AC1-AC6\" string is spec-mandated AC5 and the bash test cannot cover AC1 — repo mapping — which lives in prompt 2), but the prompt can make the labels coherent.\n*Fix:* in req 2d, additionally instruct relabeling the pre-existing comment blocks to the new spec's numbering (456 stub → AC3, cap/no-PII → AC4, etc.) so the header summary and block comments agree with the spec they now cite.\n\n**R3 — REVIEW NOTE hands the executor a decision branch.**\nPrompt lines 43-44 embed a \"REVIEW NOTE ... veto this choice ... otherwise leave as-is\" hedge inside requirement 1. Even though it strongly biases toward the status quo, it presents an \"Option A or Option B, executor decides\" fork, which the project's prompt-generation rules treat as a bug (the executor should not resolve authoring judgment calls).\n*Fix:* delete the REVIEW NOTE (or move it to a prompt-review comment outside `<requirements>`), leaving the fixed decision: truncated body → best-effort `no exception entry` fallback, no dedicated fixture, reason enum frozen.\n\n**R4 — Minor summary jargon.**\nSummary bullets 2 and 14 embed output-format tokens (`file:line in function`, `basename in function`) and test jargon (`lineno-less fixture`, `AC1-AC6`), slightly outside the \"no technical jargon\" rule. The rest of the summary is plain-language. Minor.\n*Fix (optional):* rephrase bullet 2 as \"frames are always emitted when a stack trace exists, with line numbers shown when available and file 