 quo, it presents an \"Option A or Option B, executor decides\" fork, which the project's prompt-generation rules treat as a bug (the executor should not resolve authoring judgment calls).\n*Fix:* delete the REVIEW NOTE (or move it to a prompt-review comment outside `<requirements>`), leaving the fixed decision: truncated body → best-effort `no exception entry` fallback, no dedicated fixture, reason enum frozen.\n\n**R4 — Minor summary jargon.**\nSummary bullets 2 and 14 embed output-format tokens (`file:line in function`, `basename in function`) and test jargon (`lineno-less fixture`, `AC1-AC6`), slightly outside the \"no technical jargon\" rule. The rest of the summary is plain-language. Minor.\n*Fix (optional):* rephrase bullet 2 as \"frames are always emitted when a stack trace exists, with line numbers shown when available and file names alone otherwise\", and bullet 14 as \"the deterministic mock test gains two new event fixtures and reports all assertions passing\".\n\n## Strengths\n- The inlined python block, fixtures, and assertions are verbatim-loadable and were verified to work end-to-end (I patched copies and the full suite passed) — no hallucinated symbols, no quoting hazards (the block contains no single quotes to clash with the `python3 -c '...'` wrapper), and the de-indentation instructions are explicit and correct.\n- Outstanding boundary-contract coverage: the new reason strings, the single-line guarantee, the no-PII invariant, and the schema-drift path are all exercised through the real production path (fixture server → curl → python → stdout → grep), not shape tests.\n- Precise anchors everywhere (method names, `frames_rc`/`frames` shell semantics, `check_failure`, `event_latest` 999-branch) — nothing line-number-bound.\n- The `metadata()` reuse claim for issues 222/333 was verified true (the fixture server serves any numeric id), so the fixture insertions need no server-side changes.\n- Correctly container-autonomous and correctly scoped to prompt 1 of the spec's decomposition; the operator live probe stays in the spec, and prompt 2 covers the repo-mapping ACs and appends its own changelog entry.\n- Constraints faithfully mirror the spec, including the frozen reason enum and explicit \"do NOT commit\".\n\n## Summary\nAn exemplary, fully container-executable prompt: all DoD sections present, every code reference verified against source, failure modes and security concerns covered, and — critically — the inlined code, fixtures, and assertions were reproduced verbatim in temp copies and the resulting `bash scripts/test-sentry-read.sh` passed with `PASS: all AC1-AC6 assertions passed`. The only findings are quality-level: the new mixed-lineno precedence branch has no locking fixture (R1), the test's AC labels will be inconsistent with the retargeted spec header (R2), and the REVIEW NOTE hedge in requirement 1 should be resolved to a single decision (R3). Approve after addressing R1 (and optionally R2/R3)."}],"resolvedModel":"deepseek-v4-flash[1m]","totalDurationMs":275461,"totalTokens":69353,"totalToolUseCount":21,"usage":{"input_tokens":66,"cache_creation_input_tokens":768,"cache_read_input_tokens":62464,"output_tokens":6055,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":5,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":16,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
